UnitFlow
Privacy Policy
Effective Date: May 8, 2026

1. Overview
Thank you for using UnitFlow, a unit conversion application developed for iOS. This Privacy Policy explains how UnitFlow handles information when you use our app. We are committed to protecting your privacy and being transparent about our practices.
The short version: UnitFlow does not collect, store, transmit, or share any personal data or information about you. Ever.
2. Information We Collect
UnitFlow does not collect any information from you. Specifically, we do not collect:
Personal identification information (name, email, phone number, etc.)
Device identifiers or advertising IDs
Usage data or analytics
Location data
Crash reports or diagnostic data
Any input you enter into the app (conversion values, etc.)

3. How Your Data Is Used
Because UnitFlow collects no data, there is no data to use, process, analyze, or share. All unit conversions are performed entirely on your device and are never transmitted anywhere.
4. Third-Party Services
UnitFlow does not integrate any third-party analytics, advertising, tracking, or data collection SDKs. We do not share information with any third parties because no information is collected in the first place.
5. Data Storage and Security
UnitFlow stores no user data on our servers because we have no servers involved in the app's operation. Any preferences you configure within the app (such as favorite units or display settings) are stored locally on your device only and are never transmitted to us or anyone else.
6. Children's Privacy
UnitFlow is safe for users of all ages. Because we do not collect any data, UnitFlow fully complies with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and Apple's guidelines regarding apps used by children. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone, including children under the age of 13.
7. Apple and the App Store
UnitFlow is distributed through the Apple App Store. Apple may collect certain information as part of your use of their platform and services, independent of UnitFlow. Please refer to Apple's Privacy Policy at https://www.apple.com/privacy/ for details on their data practices.
8. Changes to This Privacy Policy
If we ever update this Privacy Policy — for example, if we add new features that involve data collection — we will update the Effective Date at the top of this document and notify users through the App Store update notes. We encourage you to review this policy periodically.
Any future data collection will always be clearly disclosed and, where required by law, will require your explicit consent.
9. Your Rights
Since UnitFlow collects no personal data, there is nothing to access, correct, export, or delete. You have complete control of your experience with UnitFlow at all times.
If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA), United Kingdom, or California, you may have additional rights under applicable privacy law (GDPR, UK GDPR, or CCPA). Because we collect no personal data, these rights are automatically satisfied.
10. Contact Us
If you have any questions, concerns, or feedback about this Privacy Policy or UnitFlow's privacy practices, please contact us at jamesroche1982@icloud.com. We welcome your questions and will respond promptly.
